What was modified
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is **not** a redistribution of that project under its own name.
Per ADR-0005 it is an independent fork: the upstream tree is pinned as a
read-only clone under `upstream/`, never edited, never committed, and read at
build time by `platform/ingest/`. Everything outside `upstream/` — the schema,
the parsers, the wiki generator, the API, the site, the i18n runtime, the render
harness and the gates — was written here.

Apache-2.0 §4(b) requires modified files to carry prominent notices of change,
and §4(d) requires this NOTICE to be carried forward. The upstream attribution
above is kept for that reason.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Remotion (https://www.remotion.dev) — the render engine, used by
`platform/render/run.py`. Its licence is free for individuals and for companies
of up to three people and paid above that; this repository is rendered by an
individual, so the free tier applies. See `docs/monetization/0002-blocking-issues.md`.

PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 — `video-talkcraft`, a sibling skill. It is read for
ideas and its techniques were re-implemented; the tool itself is not shipped and
not delivered commercially. See `docs/monetization/0002-blocking-issues.md`.

Mixkit Free License — the SFX and BGM under `assets/audio/`. Attribution is
recorded in `assets/audio/ATTRIBUTION.md`. Five files in that set have no
traceable source and are marked `commercial_ok = 0`; they must be replaced before
any client-facing delivery.

`cinematique` — the MIT-licensed source of the 150-entry cinematography catalog
under `data/cinematic/`, imported by `platform/catalog/import_cinematique.py`.
See ADR-0007.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A note on the brand
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The name in the topbar, the manifest, the icons, the structured data and the
social cards is `shotcraft`. The name `video-shotcraft` belongs to the upstream
project and to its author, and where a page still shows it that is either an
attribution to the upstream work or a defect — `platform/site/check_seo.py`
treats it as the latter.